ne marrow cell morphology\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Therapy-Related Myeloid Neoplasm / Secondary AML:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs AML, Not Otherwise Specified (NOS):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: chest pain, cough, dyspnea, hemoptysis\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (APL):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal bleeding, abnormal granulocytopoietic cell morphology, acute promyelocytic leukemia, alcoholism\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs CML Blast Crisis – Myeloid Type:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal/excessive bleeding, anemia, bone pain, confusion\n\nPrimary Myelofibrosis vs Therapy-Related Myeloid Neoplasm / Secondary AML:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anti-thyroglobulin antibody positivity\n\nPrimary Myelofibrosis vs AML, Not Otherwise Specified (NOS):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n  Favours second: chest pain, cough, dyspnea, hemoptysis, weight loss\n\nPrimary Myelofibrosis vs Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (APL):\n  Favours first:  abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal granulocytopoietic cell morphology, acute promyelocytic leukemia, alcoholism, balance problems\n\nPrimary Myelofibrosis vs CML Blast Crisis – Myeloid Type:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal/excessive bleeding, anemia, bone pain, confusion\n\nTherapy-Related Myeloid Neoplasm / Secondary AML vs AML, Not Otherwise Specified (NOS):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: chest pain, cough, dyspnea, fatigue, hemoptysis\n\nTherapy-Related Myeloid Neoplasm / Secondary AML vs Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (APL):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anti-thyroglobulin antibody positivity\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal bleeding, abnormal granulocytopoietic cell morphology, acute promyelocytic leukemia, alcoholism\n\nTherapy-Related Myeloid Neoplasm / Secondary AML vs CML Blast Crisis – Myeloid Type:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal/excessive bleeding, anemia, bone pain, confusion\n\nAML, Not Otherwise Specified (NOS) vs Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (APL):\n  Favours first:  chest pain, cough, dyspnea, hemoptysis\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal bleeding, abnormal granulocytopoietic cell morphology, acute promyelocytic leukemia, alcoholism"}
